      <strong>Sea planning default:</strong> Shanghai, Ningbo-Zhoushan and Shenzhen to a transit gateway
      are recorded at roughly 30–38 days on the current Cape routing, then ~2–5 days inland to Vienna for
      a ~32–43-day door-to-door window. Rail is roughly 18–22 days to Vienna. Both are planning estimates,
      not carrier promises — for air, express or a specific door-to-door move, request a routing quote
      before committing to a date.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>4. Sea vs rail vs air: Austria's true door-to-door decision</h2>
      <p>
        In a port country you can compare a port-to-port sea quote with a rail quote. In landlocked
        Austria you cannot — <strong>"sea" always means "sea plus inland"</strong>, because the container
        must leave the transit gateway and travel roughly 480–1,000 km to Vienna before clearance and
        delivery. The honest comparison is therefore door-to-door, not port-to-port: roughly
        <strong>32–43 days</strong> for sea-plus-inland against <strong>18–22 days</strong> for rail.
      </p>

      <DataTable
        columns={[
          { key: 'mode', label: 'Mode' },
          { key: 'bestFor', label: 'Best for' },
          { key: 'indicativeTime', label: 'Indicative time' },
          { key: 'indicativeCost', label: 'Indicative cost' },
          { key: 'confidence', label: 'Confidence', type: 'confidence' },
        ]}
