        caption="Decision support for the landlocked route. Sea FCL/LCL and rail transit are MEDIUM confidence; rail, air and express dollar figures are LOW confidence or request-for-quote."
      />
      <SourceList sources={modeSources} title="Sources — sea vs rail vs air decision" />

      <div class="note mt-2">
        <strong>Critical point — the rail premium does not pay for itself on financing alone:</strong>
        rail saves roughly 14–20 days (18–22 versus ~32–43 door-to-door) at roughly 2–3× the sea rate. At
        an 8% cost of capital a $50,000 container costs ≈ $11/day in transit, so ~14 days is only about
        <strong>$154 of financing saved</strong> — which alone does not pay the rail premium. Rail is
        justified instead by <strong>stockout avoidance and market timing</strong> on high-value or
        seasonal cargo. Air is the extreme-time option, with no verified Austrian rate or transit
        published, so request that as an itemised quote rather than assuming a neighbouring airport figure.
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3 mt-2">
        <Card title="Choose sea when...">
          <ul>
            <li>Cost per kg matters more than the ~32–43-day door-to-door window.</li>
            <li>The cargo is heavy, palletised or container-sized and can plan ahead.</li>
            <li>You can accept the gateway-to-Vienna inland leg and its extra fee.</li>
          </ul>
        </Card>
        <Card title="Choose rail when...">
          <ul>
            <li>Vienna is the destination and stockouts or seasonal windows are the risk.</li>
            <li>You need roughly 18–22 days instead of ~32–43.</li>
            <li>You accept roughly 2–3× sea cost for ~14–20 days of time saved.</li>
          </ul>
        </Card>
        <Card title="Choose air when...">
          <ul>
            <li>The cargo is time-critical, light or high-value.</li>
            <li>The value of a missed sale exceeds the air premium.</li>
            <li>You have a per-kg quote that beats the cost of delay.</li>
          </ul>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>5. Ports: China origin ports and Austria's transit gateways</h2>
